From f46436faa6d7161623ffb257c0acdd838fd7a2e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias <ruck.tobias@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jul 2024 18:10:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Use=20DOGE=20and=20=C2=B5DOGE=20unit=20insted?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20of=20BCHA=20and=20XEC=20(#31)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dogecoin has 8 decimal places by default and the DOGE ticker.

To not break all tests, we add the -usedogeunit command line flag, which is similar to -ecash, except it is on by default, and changes the units to 8 places (without affecting the address prefix), and then we disable -usedoge=0 on the test framework.

